How to read this table: keep a feature idea only if it earns a '^'. Ideas that show '~' cost
complexity for no measurable gain. Also compare the two models: the same feature can help one model
family and not the other, so always ablate per model. Target encoding is designed for HIGH cardinality; with 30 cities
one-hot is just as good. Experiment: get_dataset('customers', refresh=True, n_cities=500) and re-run
(in the author's test target-encoding edged one-hot by ~0.005 AUC - small, within noise; the benefit
is expected to grow as categories get rarer, and one-hot's column count explodes).


